PUBLIC RESPONSE: {B}

The ESA requires employers with 25+ employees (counted as of 1 Jan each year) to maintain written policies on disconnecting from work (due by 1 Mar of that year) and electronic monitoring (in force since Oct 2022). A copy of each policy must be given to every employee within 30 days of preparation/revision and to every new hire within 30 days of hire.  

Option B is the only choice that explicitly violates the distribution obligation: the employer has the required policies yet refuses to give them to new employees. All other options either fall below the 25-employee threshold on the relevant January 1 date (so no policy is required) or meet both the content and distribution rules. Therefore B is not in compliance as of 2 Jan 2023.}

